title: The Hamburg Mandates
subtitle: The mandate commission must say who may vote.
view-if: congress = 1 and congress_heidelberg = 1 and congress_closing = 0 and heid_cg_mandates = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.heid_cg_mandates = 1;
RG.congress.tally();
!}
frequency: 400
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: congress

= The Hamburg Mandates

The fight over the theses starts as a fight over paper. The mandate commission, chaired by Wilhelm Pieck, has the credentials of the Hamburg and Bremen delegations on the table. Hamburg elected its delegates at a mass meeting nobody from the Zentrale was allowed to address; Bremen sent men who have not paid dues to the Zentrale since the spring. [? if heid_mandates = 1 : The Left Radicals already say that the mandates were drawn up to beat them. ?][? if heid_mandates = 0 : The mandates were freely elected, and the Left Radicals want the commission to say so. ?]

Laufenberg tells the commission that if Hamburg's delegates are struck off, Hamburg will draw its own conclusions.

- @annul: Strike off the irregular mandates.
- @consult: Seat them with a voice, but no vote.
- @seat: Seat them in full, and beat them in the debate.
- @vote: Let the whole congress vote on the mandates.

@annul
subtitle: The Spartacist commission does its duty. Many of their votes vanish; the split will be uglier.
on-arrival: {!
var n = RG.congress.annul('hamburg', 'ultraleft', 0.6) + RG.congress.annul('bremen', 'ultraleft', 0.5);
Q.congress_last_moved = n;
RG.congress.bitter(6);
Q.unity -= 5;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 10;
Q.heid_split_share = Math.min(0.85, Q.heid_split_share + 0.05);
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
RG.district('hamburg', {loyalty: -10});
RG.district('bremen', {loyalty: -8});
!}

The commission finds that the Hamburg and Bremen meetings were improperly called. [? if congress_last_moved > 0 : [+ congress_last_moved +] Left Radical delegates lose their votes and watch from the back of the room. ?][? if congress_last_moved = 0 : It turns out that few of the delegates it can strike off were Left Radicals anyway. ?] Our side now has [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall. In Hamburg, the story will be told for years.

@consult
subtitle: A lawyer's answer. Fewer of their votes are lost, and fewer tempers.
on-arrival: {!
var n = RG.congress.annul('hamburg', 'ultraleft', 0.3) + RG.congress.annul('bremen', 'ultraleft', 0.25);
Q.congress_last_moved = n;
RG.congress.bitter(3);
Q.unity -= 2;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 4;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

Hamburg and Bremen may speak as long as they like. [? if congress_last_moved > 0 : [+ congress_last_moved +] of their delegates may not vote. ?] Our side now has [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall.

@seat
subtitle: Party democracy. It costs votes now, and it may win the argument later.
on-arrival: {!
Q.unity += 4;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction += 6;
Q.heid_split_share = Math.max(0.55, Q.heid_split_share - 0.05);
RG.congress.sway(0.03);
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

Every delegate is seated. The Left Radicals, who expected to be robbed, are disarmed for an evening. [? if congress_last_moved > 0 : [+ congress_last_moved +] waverers are impressed enough to come over to us. ?] Our side has [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall.

@vote
subtitle: Whoever wins the test vote very likely wins the congress. A gamble.
on-arrival: {!
var n = 0;
if (Q.congress_ahead) {
    n = RG.congress.annul('hamburg', 'ultraleft', 0.45);
    RG.congress.sway(0.02);
    RG.congress.bitter(3);
} else {
    RG.congress.lose(0.04);
}
RG.congress.tally();
Q.congress_last_moved = n;
!}

[? if congress_last_moved > 0 : The test vote goes our way, and [+ congress_last_moved +] Hamburg mandates are struck off by the congress itself. Nobody can call it the commission's fix. ?][? if congress_last_moved = 0 : The congress votes to seat Hamburg in full, and the waverers notice who lost. ?] Our side has [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall.
